  if you're using the same file at the  same time you're going to have  conflicted copies where here I can edit  it at the same time that GEOMAR and  Gretchen are editing it and it's easy to  be able to you know have those changes  and keep them updated I'll show you  another one this is a DC was my  programmer so this is slightly different  things so we are always updating new  tasks so with your mark Gretchen it's  more habitual things certain processes  that have to be done every day or every  week every month and with a decent  programmer we're looking at new things  that have to be done on an ongoing basis  as we're developing new features for our  website so what happens here is I'll  make a list and this goes on and on and  on  we all have the to dues that we want to  get done for our website and then we  have to kind of prioritize them and so  basically what he says every day is he  logs into the Google Drive here and  looks at what's number one on the list  and they'll start working his way  through so I will add these projects to  the list and then when he's done he'll  click on he'll add done here so I know  that it's done and I can take a look and  I will be yourself so for removing  things from the list so we have it set  that I'm the only one who adds to the  list and also removes from the list and  so you know he'll click done and so I  can always check it out before it gets  removed and if we have any comments here  we can add it in and we can easily talk  about it together so I'll try to explain  what I want and hopefully that makes  sense and if it doesn't then he can add  some comments in as well and he simply  starts working through that list task by  task and so I found it to be just so  much easier than using something like  Basecamp because you just add to the  file and we could put in priority and he  just starts hammering away on these  every day when he logs into his computer  so that's the first reason I signed up  for Google Drive and it'